 "description": "BIGVILLE R23 (block 271000) -- FERTILITY: the quantity-quality decision as a GRAPH DECISION, NEVER keyed on wealth. Three staged one-shot rules: bf_oldage (oldage_motive = safety_net?0:oldage_value -- the old-age-security insurance motive, R9), bf_quantity_quality (decision_value = base_target + child_labour_benefit + oldage_motive - school_cost - opp_cost; desired_surviving = max(floor, decision_value) -- the Becker quantity-quality tradeoff, R18 school + mother opp cost), bf_mortality_replace (survival = max(eps, 1-mortality); fertility = desired_surviving / survival -- the demographic-transition replacement, ties R22 child mortality). `fertility` is a desired-births RATE; birth stays the honest R14 ingest boundary but GATED by this decision. NO wealth/coin/class attr is read by ANY rule: the wealth->fertility gradient, if any, must come THROUGH the mechanism inputs (the anti-tuning source-audit). NO reward/punishment token. Composes existing DSL Terms; ZERO new Rust.",
